# Kimi K2.8 Preview — findings by GLM 5.3 (SELF-EXCLUDED)

- Source: Moonshot AI (`moonshot/kimi-k2-8-preview`)
- Date: 2026-09-24 (UTC)
- Overview and scoring methodology: `../../model-comparison.md`
- Cross-model signed log: `../../model-findings.md`

## Negative findings (why this file is `.excluded`)

**ZERO verified public benchmark numbers were found for this exact model/ID.** Per the self-exclusion rule this file is saved as `GLM_5.3.md.excluded` — no scored `.md` is written, and no placeholder scores are invented.

What was verified (platform/curated metadata only, no measured numbers):

- **Identity:** Kimi K2.8 Preview — Moonshot AI's mid-tier coding and agentic model inside Kimi Code, positioned between K2.7 Code and flagship K3.
- **Specs (curated):** 1M (1,048,576) context; text/image in; text out; efficient reasoning.
- **Pricing (curated):** Kimi membership plan (no per-token billing, no Zen Free ID — not on the OpenCode Zen list at all).

Sources checked with no benchmark rows for this ID (2026-09-24):

- BenchLM (`kimi-k2-8-preview`): not found (404). The Moonshot family pages cover K2.6 / K2.5 / K2.7 Code / K2 / K3 only.
- Artificial Analysis: no page (404).
- BenchmarkList: no page (404).
- LLMReference: no page (404).
- Hugging Face `moonshotai/Kimi-K2.8-Preview`: gated (401) — no public model card/benchmarks.
- OpenCode Zen docs (2026-09-24): Kimi K3, K2.7 Code, K2.6 listed; K2.8 Preview absent.

Interpolation between verified siblings (K2.7 Code ≈ 50.4 BenchLM, K3 ≈ 72.5) was deliberately NOT used to fabricate dimension scores.

**Re-research update (2026-10-17, second deep pass — still excluded, but materially richer negative findings):**

- Official Kimi Code What's New page (fetched 2026-10-17) confirms the 2026-09-11 rollout facts: model ID unchanged (`kimi-for-coding`), performance "close to K3" with more efficient thinking, effort low/high/max (default max), 1M context across tiers, and a routing rule: no-thinking requests to the K3 series and K2.8 are served by K2.8 Preview (no thinking). Still NO benchmark table anywhere in the changelog.
- Independent guide (ki-ai.chat, revised 2026-09-30) — the first substantive third-party evidence, but hands-on rather than standardized benchmarks: a JavaScript slugify-repair session in Kimi Code CLI 0.43.0 passed 4/4 original + 12/12 held-out tests, editing only the permitted source file (one successful repair, not an autonomous-run benchmark); Chat-side observations (K2.8 High, tools enabled): an order-card/table/chart image exercise returned **25/26 fields literally correct** with no invented values; a 20-answer documentation search run had 17 confirmed / 1 partial / 2 unresolved (neither response flagged conflicting official sources); a Memory workflow matched 12/12 values across probes.
- Access/pricing verified by the same guide: Code API endpoints `https://api.kimi.ai/coding/v1` (overseas, OpenAI- and Anthropic-compatible) and `https://api.kimi.com/coding/v1` (China); membership-bundled (Plus $19 / Pro $39 / Max $99 / Ultra $199 per month), **not** per-token; current Plus gets K2.8's 1M window while K3 needs Pro+ for 1M — an access distinction, not a quality ranking (guide's own caveat).
- Hugging Face `moonshotai/Kimi-K2.8-Preview`: still gated (401, re-checked 2026-10-17) — no public weights, model card, or parameter count; the guide explicitly finds no weight release and no standalone Global-API K2.8 ID (catalog rechecked 2026-09-30).
- BenchLM (`kimi-k2-8-preview` and slug variants): still 404.

Verdict unchanged: hands-on review evidence exists now, but every standardized row (SWE-bench, GPQA, HLE, Terminal-Bench, etc.) still reads "no verified public score found" — a single repair test plus image/search/memory observations cannot honestly populate dimension scores. A future re-research should look for (a) a public K2.8 model card or Moonshot blog with official numbers, (b) aggregation-site coverage once the preview graduates, (c) a weight release or standalone Global-API ID with per-token pricing — then write a fresh `GLM_5.3.md`.

